Table full name: HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS.HUMAN_GENOME_VARIANTS._1000_GENOMES_SAMPLE_INFO
Column name: In_Exon_Targetted_Pilot Type: BOOLEAN Description: The Sample is in the exon targetted pilot experiment
Column name: Has_Sequence_in_Phase1 Type: BOOLEAN Description: Has sequence low coverage sequence in the 20101123.sequence.index file or exome sequence in the 20110522 sequence index file
Column name: LC_Indel_Ratio Type: FLOAT Description: Both Indel ratios are the ratio of insertions to deletions found in that sample using a quick test (based on samtools). If the ratio is higher than 5 the sample is withdrawn.
Column name: LC_Passed_QC Type: BOOLEAN Description: These are binary flags showing if the sample passed QC, All samples which have passed QC have bam files. Only samples which have both exome and low coverage data are found under ftp/data and listed in the standard alignment index. The small number of other samples are found in ftp://ftp.1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/ftp/technical/phase3_EX_or_LC_only_alignment/
Column name: VerifyBam_E_Omni_Free Type: FLOAT Description: Value from UMich's VerifyBamID BAM QC program http://genome.sph.umich.edu/wiki/VerifyBamID.  The Free measures use a statistical model based on the haplotypes discovered by the chip. The Chip measure considers the genotypes available for that individual from that chip. We use greater than 3% as a cut off for our our low coverage samples and greater than 3.5% for our exome samples.
Column name: Gender Type: TEXT Description: Gender
Column name: DNA_Source_from_Coriell Type: TEXT Description: This was the annotated DNA Source from Coriell     
Column name: Non_Paternity Type: TEXT Description: sample ids for annotated non paternal relationships
Column name: VerifyBam_E_Affy_Free Type: FLOAT Description: Value from UMich's VerifyBamID BAM QC program http://genome.sph.umich.edu/wiki/VerifyBamID.  The Free measures use a statistical model based on the haplotypes discovered by the chip. The Chip measure considers the genotypes available for that individual from that chip. We use greater than 3% as a cut off for our our low coverage samples and greater than 3.5% for our exome samples.
Column name: In_Low_Coverage_Pilot Type: BOOLEAN Description: The sample is in the low coverage pilot experiment
Column name: Has_Affy_6_0_Genotypes Type: BOOLEAN Description: Affy 6.0 Genotypes in  ftp://ftp.1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/ftp/technical/working/20121128_corriel_p3_sample_genotypes/
Column name: Total_LC_Sequence Type: FLOAT Description: The total amount of low coverage sequence available
Column name: LC_Non_Duplicated_Aligned_Coverage Type: FLOAT Description: The non duplicated aligned coverage for the low coverage sequence data.  This was calculated using the ftp://ftp.1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/ftp/alignment_indices/20130502.low_coverage.alignment.index.bas.gz file, the (mapped bases - duplicated bases) was summed for each sample and divided by 2.75GB and rounded to 2dp
Column name: Main_project_LC_Centers Type: TEXT Description: low coverage sequencing centers for final sequencing round
Column name: In_Final_Phase_Variant_Calling Type: BOOLEAN Description: Any sample which has both LC and E QC passed bams is in the final analysis set
Column name: Sample Type: TEXT Description: Sample ID
Column name: VerifyBam_LC_Omni_Chip Type: FLOAT Description: Value from UMich's VerifyBamID BAM QC program http://genome.sph.umich.edu/wiki/VerifyBamID.  The Free measures use a statistical model based on the haplotypes discovered by the chip. The Chip measure considers the genotypes available for that individual from that chip. We use greater than 3% as a cut off for our our low coverage samples and greater than 3.5% for our exome samples.
Column name: Population_Description Type: TEXT Description: Description of Population
Column name: HC_Pilot_Centers Type: TEXT Description: high coverage sequencing centers
Column name: X_Targets_Covered_to_20x_or_greater Type: FLOAT Description: The percentage of targets covered to 20x or greater as calculated by the picard function CalculateHsMetrics using these targets ftp://ftp.1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/ftp/technical/reference/exome_pull_down_targets_phases1_and_2/20120518.consensus.annotation.bed
Column name: Phase1_LC_Platform Type: TEXT Description: phase1 low coverage sequencing platforms
Column name: Has_Axiom_Genotypes Type: BOOLEAN Description: Axiom Genotypes in ftp://ftp.1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/ftp/technical/working/20110210_Affymetrix_Axiom/Affymetrix_Axiom_DB_2010_v4_b37.vcf.gz         
Column name: ET_Pilot_Centers Type: TEXT Description: exon targetted sequencing centers,
Column name: In_High_Coverage_Pilot Type: BOOLEAN Description: The sample is in the high coverage pilot
Column name: ET_Pilot_Platforms Type: TEXT Description: exon targetted sequencing platforms,
Column name: Relationship Type: TEXT Description: Relationship to other members of the family
Column name: Super_Population Type: TEXT Description: From ftp://ftp.1000genomes.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/ftp/20131219.superpopulations.tsv
Column name: Third_Order Type: TEXT Description: sample ids for any third order cryptic relations. As mentioned above, this analysis was not as widely run as the other relatedness analyses and as such there may still be unannotated third order relations in the set
Column name: Population Type: TEXT Description: 3 letter population code
Column name: Main_Project_E_Platform Type: TEXT Description: Exome sequencing platform for the final sequencing round
Column name: Siblings Type: TEXT Description: sample ids for any siblings
Column name: Has_phase1_chrY_Deletions Type: BOOLEAN Description: The sample is genotyepd in the chrY phase1 deletions
Column name: Half_Siblings Type: TEXT Description: sample ids for any half siblings
Column name: Grandparents Type: TEXT Description: sample ids for any grand parents
Column name: VerifyBam_E_Affy_Chip Type: FLOAT Description: Value from UMich's VerifyBamID BAM QC program http://genome.sph.umich.edu/wiki/VerifyBamID.  The Free measures use a statistical model based on the haplotypes discovered by the chip. The Chip measure considers the genotypes available for that individual from that chip. We use greater than 3% as a cut off for our our low coverage samples and greater than 3.5% for our exome samples.
