Column name: HaplotypeScore Type: FLOAT Description: Approximate read depth (reads with MQ=255 or with bad mates are filtered)
Column name: RU Type: TEXT Description: Z-score from Wilcoxon rank sum test of Alt Vs. Ref base qualities
Column name: call Type: VARIANT Description: Maximum likelihood expectation (MLE) for the allele counts (not necessarily the same as the AC), for each ALT allele, in the same order as listed
Column name: alternate_bases Type: VARIANT Description: One record for each alternate base (if any).
Column name: BaseCounts Type: VARIANT Description: Variant names (e.g. RefSNP ID).
Column name: partition_date_please_ignore Type: DATE Description: Were any of the samples downsampled?
Column name: end_position Type: NUMBER Description: End position (0-based). Corresponds to the first base after the last base in the reference allele.
Column name: reference_bases Type: TEXT Description: Reference bases.
Column name: MQ0 Type: NUMBER Description: filter level in range 0-9 or no value (non-integer: N,?) with zero being least reliable; to threshold at FL=n, use all levels n-9
Column name: quality Type: FLOAT Description: Allele count in genotypes, for each ALT allele, in the same order as listed
Column name: Dels Type: FLOAT Description: Genotype of the call. "-1" is used in cases where the genotype is not called.
Column name: DP Type: NUMBER Description: One record for each call.
Column name: GC Type: FLOAT Description: Allelic depths for the ref and alt alleles in the order listed
Column name: AN Type: NUMBER Description: Maximum likelihood expectation (MLE) for the allele frequency (not necessarily the same as the AF), for each ALT allele, in the same order as listed
Column name: InbreedingCoeff Type: FLOAT Description: Genotype Quality
Column name: MQ Type: FLOAT Description: Normalized, Phred-scaled likelihoods for genotypes as defined in the VCF specification
Column name: FS Type: FLOAT Description: Phaseset of the call (if any). "*" is used in cases where the genotype is phased, but no phase set ("PS" in FORMAT) was specified.
